; Supply-chain guard for lockfile generation (requires npm >= 11.10).
; npm refuses to resolve package versions published less than 3 days ago when
; you run `npm install` / refresh package-lock.json, giving researchers and
; scanners time to catch malicious releases (also covers transitive deps).
; Renovate adds its own PR cooldowns on top: 3 days (patch), 7 (minor),
; 14 (major); security advisory fixes are never delayed.
; `npm ci` (used by CI) installs the already-vetted lockfile and is NOT
; affected, so builds never break because of this setting.
; Transient exceptions go here instead of disabling the guard:
;   npm config set min-release-age-exclude '["pkg"]'
min-release-age=3
